WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.322
Non-coding RNAs regulate the cell largely through
their interactions with proteins,

00:00:05.402 --> 00:00:09.552
but mapping these interactions experimentally is
slow and costly.

00:00:09.632 --> 00:00:15.605
Most computational predictors sidestep the general
problem by training one model per protein,

00:00:15.685 --> 00:00:20.096
which requires a large interaction dataset for that
specific protein.

00:00:20.176 --> 00:00:26.474
Such datasets exist for only a few hundred of the
roughly two thousand human RNA-binding proteins.

00:00:26.554 --> 00:00:31.485
What is missing is a method that decides, for any
given RNA and protein pair,

00:00:31.565 --> 00:00:35.130
whether they interact using nothing but their sequences.
